              "text": "صيدلي (ṣaydalī) is the druggist, from ṣaydalānī. Lane's sources derive that word from a place called Ṣaydalān, or from ṣaydal, or call it a Persian word arabicized. Lane also records the by-form ṣandalānī, which points to ṣandal, \"sandalwood\"; the origin is not settled."
